    "summary": "Integer overflow in gawk's `do_sub()` can cause buffer overflow and denial of service",
    "details": "Integer overflow vulnerability has been found in \"builtin.c\" program file of gawk (`do_sub()` routine). This issue could be used to overwrite gawk heap metadata and objects causing the program to crash. It affects 32-bit builds of gawk in versions 5.4.0 and below.",
